# A Conversation with. . . Catharine R. Stimpson.

**Authors:** Cheney, Lynne V.

## Abstract
Presents a dialogue between National Endowment for the Humanities chairman, Lynne V. Cheney, and Modern Language Association president, Catharine R. Stimpson. Presents their views on literary criticism, teaching and research, feminism, the future of the humanities, and the search for enduring values in a pluralistic society. Examines the idea of a core curriculum in undergraduate study. (CH)

